              "ev-1af832f80e08-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the Court has consistently applied a rational\u2011basis test to determine whether a congressional objective is likely to advance a legitimate governmental purpose."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1af832f80e08b1353f2f3283b8b038009c165c1ffa36ab0520c637ed7c4c6607",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1af832f80e08-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, the statute at issue requires the government to detain lawful permanent\u2011resident aliens not because they pose a flight risk, but because they have been convicted of certain crimes."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Source",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1af832f80e08b1353f2f3283b8b038009c165c1ffa36ab0520c637ed7c4c6607",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1af832f80e08-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Eighty\u2011five percent of aliens placed in removal proceedings do not challenge the immigration decision, and more than half of those cases are resolved within thirty days."
      }
